      { "sa": "ucyate", "en": "is called" }
    ],
    "translation": "What is that brahman? What is that which concerns the self? What is action, O highest of persons? And what is declared to be that which concerns beings? What is called that which concerns the gods?"
  },
  "2": {
    "words": [
      { "sa": "adhiyajñaḥ", "en": "what concerns sacrifice" },
      { "sa": "katham", "en": "how" },
      { "sa": "kaḥ", "en": "who" },
      { "sa": "atra", "en": "here" },
      { "sa": "dehe", "en": "in the body" },
      { "sa": "asmin", "en": "in this" },
      { "sa": "madhu-sūdana", "en": "O slayer of Madhu" },
      { "sa": "prayāṇa-kāle", "en": "at the time of departure" },
      { "sa": "ca", "en": "and" },
      { "sa": "katham", "en": "how" },
      { "sa": "jñeyaḥ", "en": "to be known" },
      { "sa": "asi", "en": "you are" },
      { "sa": "niyata-ātmabhiḥ", "en": "by those of controlled self", "term": "atman" }
    ],
    "translation": "Who is that which concerns sacrifice, and how is it here in this body, O slayer of Madhu? And how are you to be known at the time of departure by those of controlled self?"
  },
  "3": {
    "words": [
      { "sa": "akṣaram", "en": "the imperishable" },
      { "sa": "brahma", "en": "brahman", "term": "brahman" },
      { "sa": "paramam", "en": "the highest" },
      { "sa": "svabhāvaḥ", "en": "one's own nature" },
      { "sa": "adhyātmam", "en": "what concerns the self", "term": "atman" },
      { "sa": "ucyate", "en": "is called" },
      { "sa": "bhūta-bhāva-udbhava-karaḥ", "en": "causing the arising of the states of beings" },
      { "sa": "visargaḥ", "en": "the sending forth" },
      { "sa": "karma-saṁjñitaḥ", "en": "named action", "term": "karma" }
    ],
    "translation": "Brahman is the imperishable, the highest. One's own nature is called that which concerns the self. The sending forth that causes the arising of the states of beings is named action.",
    "notes": ["\"The sending forth\" can also be read as \"the offering\", meaning the act of giving in sacrifice."]
  },
  "4": {
    "words": [
      { "sa": "adhibhūtam", "en": "what concerns beings" },
      { "sa": "kṣaraḥ", "en": "perishable" },
      { "sa": "bhāvaḥ", "en": "existence" },
      { "sa": "puruṣaḥ", "en": "the person" },
      { "sa": "ca", "en": "and" },
      { "sa": "adhidaivatam", "en": "what concerns the gods" },
      { "sa": "adhiyajñaḥ", "en": "what concerns sacrifice" },
      { "sa": "aham", "en": "I" },
      { "sa": "eva", "en": "alone" },
      { "sa": "atra", "en": "here" },
      { "sa": "dehe", "en": "in the body" },
      { "sa": "deha-bhṛtām", "en": "of those who bear a body" },
      { "sa": "vara", "en": "O best" }
    ],
    "translation": "That which concerns beings is perishable existence, and the person is that which concerns the gods. That which concerns sacrifice is I alone, here in the body, O best of those who bear a body."
  },
  "5": {
    "words": [
